 social media management, Alumni App promotion, analytics, and alumni event support, the intern helps deliver digital and in person experiences that encourage lifelong learning, meaningful connections, and active participation across the IMD alumni network. Key activities & accountabilities Support the IAA and alumni team as it drives adoption of the new IMD Alumni App, a digital platform for alumni engagement. Create and schedule content for alumni social media channels, including LinkedIn, Instagram, and the IMD Alumni App. Assist with the management and promotion of the IMD Alumni App, including content updates, user engagement campaigns, and analytics tracking. Assist alumni with troubleshooting. Monitor social media performance and prepare monthly engagement reports. Support digital marketing efforts for alumni events, reunions, and webinars. Stay abreast of social media and community engagement trends and recommend new ideas to enhance alumni participation. Support alumni events, especially alumni reunions and post on social media. Formula for success Education Current student or recent graduate in Marketing, Communications, Digital Media, Business, or a related field. Ideal Profile Strong writing and communication skills in English. Experience working in an international environment is a strong plus Demonstrated organizational and administration skills Ability to handle multiple priorities in an independent manner Customer-oriented How to apply If you have the above skills and would like to work in our stimulating environment, please send your complete application file (letter of motivation and resume in English, copies of your work certificates and diplomas). If you’re a qualified candidate with a disability (such as dyslexia, sight and/or hearing disabilities, etc) and you need a reasonable accommodation in order to apply for this position, please specify it in your application. A valid Swiss work permit or Swiss or EU-25EFTA citizenship is required for this position. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Cookie Policy Copyright Privacy © 2006-2025 IMD - International Institute for Management Development IMD complies with applicable laws and regulations, including with respect to international sanctions that may be imposed on individuals and countries. This policy applies to all applications for IMD programs from individuals or organizations, and any commercial or non-commercial partnerships. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Confirm My Choices Accept All Cookies"
