ort for the CDC and contributing to process improvements (e.g., Excel lists, student groups creation, photos, printing materials, etc.). Collecting feedback and creating surveys using Qualtrics. Managing logistical tasks such as room bookings, calendar scheduling, and related coordination. Tracking attendance at CDC events. Supporting the planning, logistics, and follow-up of CDC events (e.g., visitor badges, lunch bookings, postings, gift preparation, room signage). Maintaining and updating CDC systems (e.g., 12twenty, Canvas, Teams, Salesforce) with relevant content such as events, assignments, workshops, job opportunities, resource library items, and contact details. Assisting the CDC team with ad hoc requests and operational needs. Organising and streamlining the CDC shared folder, enhancing the structure and filing system. Developing and maintaining Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). Engaging with students in relation to logistics management and communication. Collaborating with other colleagues across CDC, Degree Programmes and IMD as a whole. Formula for success Education Currently pursuing a Bachelor's degree Experience Must be enrolled in a University for the duration of the contract Requirements Demonstrated organization and administration skills Ability to handle multiple priorities in an independent manner Strong interpersonal and written communication skills Team player is a must, as you will work closely to other members of the MBA office Stress management, customer-oriented, professional Time management, organization, and logistics skills Diplomatic and discreet, proactive Excellent English Computer literate How to apply If you have the above skills and would like to work in our stimulating environment, please send your complete application file (letter of motivation and resume in English, copies of your work certificates and diplomas). If you’re a qualified candidate with a disability (such as dyslexia, sight and/or hearing disabilities, etc) and 