    "https://jobs.imd.org/job/Lausanne-EMBA-Student-Experience-Coordinator-Intern/1373287857/": {
      "title": "EMBA Student Experience Coordinator Intern",
      "description": "EMBA Student Experience Coordinator Intern Job Details | IMD We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View All Jobs View profile View All Jobs View profile View All Jobs View profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Job Family All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » EMBA Student Experience Coordinator Intern Contract Type: Fixed-term maximal Location: Lausanne, CH About IMD The International Institute for Management Development (IMD) has been pioneering leadership development for nearly 80 years. Founded by business for business, we are an independent university institute with Swiss roots and global reach. Operating from Lausanne with strategic hubs in Singapore, Shenzhen, and Cape Town, IMD works with 20,000+ executives from 120+ countries annually. Our 145,000+ alumni form a powerful global network. Consistently ranked among the world's top business schools, IMD bridges cutting-edge research with real-world application to help leaders solve problems, scale solutions, and drive impact. Real Learning for Real Impact. To reinforce our team, we are looking for an Executive MBA Student Experience Coordinator intern (100%) - 1 February – 31 July 2027 The Job's Mission IMD (Institute for Management Development) is a self-owned foundation dedicated to the development of international business executives at each stage in their careers based on the shores of Lake Geneva in Lausanne, Switzerland. Our unique environment enables us to maintain our position as a world leader in Executive Development. Our Executive MBA program is ranked among the best in the world. It helps students learn how to become more reflective global leaders, to lead with personal responsibility and integrity, while having a positive impact on their business and society. It provides a life-changing career journey with incredible networking opportunities for those with the ambition to make a real difference in a complex and rapidly changing world. We are looking for a dynamic intern to support the EMBA  Student Experience and Academic Services related operations. Our EMBA program is delivered virtually and face to-face. Key activities & accountabilities Supporting the Student Experience and Academic Services Team in the following areas: Delivery of the EMBA programs with high-level service and world-class standards Coordination of the program deliverables and gather teaching material from Faculty members and liaise with other internal departments (marketing, communication, F&B, etc.) Learning management system to support students’ learning experience Answer requests from the students during their learning journey Collaboration on process improvement initiatives to enhance efficiency and student experience Support the delivery of virtual sessions and webinars Formula for success Education Currently pursuing a bachelor’s degree in hospitality or event management Other business management certification with strong experience in a multicultural customer relations role also possible Ideal Profile Ability to handle multiple priorities in an independent manner Strong interpersonal and written communication skills Team player is a must, as you will work closely with other members of the Degree Programs department and the students Stress management, customer-oriented, professional Time management, organization, and coordination skills Diplomatic and discreet, proactive Excellent English; French and other languages are an advantage Computer literate (MS Office) How to apply If you have the above skills and would like to work in our stimulating environment, please send your complete application file (letter of motivation and resume in English, copies of your work certificates and diplomas). If you’re a qualified candidate with a disability (such as dyslexia, sight and/or hearing disabilities, etc) and you need a reasonable accommodation in order to apply for this position, please specify it in your application. A valid Swiss work permit or Swiss or EU-25EFTA citizenship is required for this position. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Cookie Policy Copyright Privacy © 2006-2025 IMD - International Institute for Management Development IMD complies with applicable laws and regulations, including with respect to international sanctions that may be imposed on individuals and countries. This policy applies to all applications for IMD programs from individuals or organizations, and any commercial or non-commercial partnerships. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Confirm My Choices Accept All Cookies"
